  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project skill and locating how the storefront cart API and merchant configuration work.The cart limit belongs in the facade that already creates and updates lines, reading the store setting on each request so a change applies without a restart.The storefront cart REST API now rejects any create, add, or quantity change that would put more than N units on a cart line. N comes from the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant configuration (default 99) and is read on each request, so a change applies without a restart. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Requests over the limit return HTTP 400 and leave the cart unchanged. The check is in `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl` for `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`, with the key in `Constants`. A non-numeric or negative setting is treated as 99.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 and unchanged cart for over-limit add, update, and multi update\", \"default of 99 when CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY is absent\", \"quantity 0 still removes a line\", \"a changed setting applies without restart\"], \"missing\": [\"a runnable cart API test or fixture that sets merchant configuration and asserts status and cart contents\"]}",
